<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds closed firmer but off session highs as traders kept to the sidelines in the absence of their U.S. counterparts, with U.S. markets closed for the Labor Day holiday.</p>
<p>&quot;Movements are very small in size because trade is thin,&quot; said a trader.</p>
<p>Most dealers expected the Bank of Spain to leave its key money market rate unchanged at 7.25 percent on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The Bank of Spain has room to cut after the Bundesbank did in its last meeting, but maybe it wants to wait for the budget,&quot; a trader said.</p>
</text>
